  "answer": "I found no earlier ticket in the archive that reports this problem. That problem is a multi-second freeze of the whole Terminal window on every input-language switch (Win+Space or Alt+Shift) when many tabs are open. The closest tickets were about other problems. #18803 is a general unresponsive-window report that turned out to be an Nvidia driver issue. #17187 is about wrong characters after a layout switch. #14349 and #18713 are about specific IMEs (the legacy Japanese IME and WeType). Please file this as a new issue. Include the controlled test of freeze duration against tab count that you offered, and a WPR/ETW trace or a dump taken during the freeze. Also say whether the freeze happens in a fresh window with only a few tabs, and whether it happens in the Canary build (https://aka.ms/terminal-canary-installer). Until it's fixed, you can reduce the freeze by splitting your tabs across several Terminal windows."
 },
